Subject: `s.replace(re, K).length` in compiled code computes the length from the match vector and makes no result string

What this does
  - new `qjs_aot_replace_len` (quickjs-aot-rt.h): for a flat string subject, a pristine RegExp and a flat replacement string without `$` (no named groups, not sticky without global), runs the same match loop as the pristine replace, sets a global RegExp's lastIndex to 0 as replace does, and returns the length of the string replace would build; 0 with nothing observable done in any other case (a match that throws clears its exception and the caller's ordinary call throws it again)
  - `qjs_aot_array_builtin_fn(2)` is String.prototype.replace, so a compiled site can identify the builtin callee by its function pointer
  - RegExp.prototype[Symbol.replace] joins the pristine snapshot (`js_regexp_snapshot`): String.prototype.replace looks it up, so a fast path that skips the lookup needs it to be the original

Why we need it
  The regexp row runs 712 `s.replace(re, K).length` sites; each made a result string only to read its length and drop it. With the generator's site (a call whose only reader is the next `.length`, profiled callee String.prototype.replace) asking for the length first: regexp row at fixed work -9.8% cycles, -10.4% instructions, stripped binary +1.4%.

Soundness
  The length is computed from the same match vector `js_regexp_replace_fast` copies spans from (same span rule, same empty-match advance), so it equals the built string's length; any condition the fast replace does not cover declines before any effect except a global RegExp's lastIndex = 0, which the ordinary call then repeats. The snapshot entry only makes `js_regexp_fast` fail when Symbol.replace was changed, which sends those calls down the generic path. Differential, compiled unit vs interpreter: 234,000 cases (13 regexps incl. empty matches and captures, 6 replacements incl. `$`, 10 subjects incl. 16-bit) and 23 guard cases (Symbol.replace patched, replaced and restored, exec patched, String.prototype.replace replaced, named groups, sticky, lastIndex global and not, subclass, own exec, String object, string pattern, function replacement, `$&`, 16-bit replacement, flags getter) are identical; the 13 Octane rows compile and run.

